.TH GLPI-CONSOLE 1 "August 2025" "GLPI 10.0.19" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
glpi-console \- Command-line interface for GLPI administration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B glpi-console
.RI [ options ] " <command> [arguments]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBglpi-console\fR command provides a command-line interface (CLI) to administer and manage a GLPI installation. It allows administrators to perform various maintenance, configuration, and automation tasks directly from the terminal, without using the web interface.

.SH COMMANDS
Commonly used commands include:
.TP
\fBglpi-console database:update\fR
Update the GLPI database schema.
.TP
\fBglpi-console user:create\fR
Create a new GLPI user.
.TP
\fBglpi-console user:list\fR
List all GLPI users.
.TP
\fBglpi-console maintenance:enable\fR
Enable maintenance mode.
.TP
\fBglpi-console maintenance:disable\fR
Disable maintenance mode.
.TP
\fBglpi-console task:run\fR
Run scheduled tasks (cron).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB--help\fR
Display help for the command.
.TP
\fB--env=ENV\fR
Specify the environment (e.g., production, development).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Update the database schema:
.B
glpi-console database:update
.TP
Create a new user:
.B
glpi-console user:create --username=admin --password=secret

.SH FILES
.TP
\fI/usr/bin/glpi-console\fR
The GLPI CLI executable.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glpi (8)

